    <string name="guide_done">Start Guarding</string>
    <string name="guide_step1_title">Your Offline Focus Shield</string>
    <string name="guide_step1_body">Warden watches visible text on your phone via Android’s Accessibility Service and sends you Home whenever a blocked distraction appears.</string>
    <string name="guide_step1_tip">100% private: scanning happens strictly on your phone. Zero analytics, zero servers.</string>
    <string name="guide_step1_cta">Enable Accessibility Permission</string>
    <string name="guide_step2_title">Blocked Words, Safe Phrases &amp; Grace</string>
    <string name="guide_step2_body">Use the Rules tab to add distracting keywords, add Safe Phrases to prevent false blocks, and tune the Grace Window.</string>
    <string name="guide_step2_tip">Example: Block “shorts”, mark “basketball shorts” as Safe, and keep Grace at 2s so fleeting mentions never interrupt you.</string>
    <string name="guide_step3_title">The Adversarial AI Gatekeeper</string>
    <string name="guide_step3_body">Need temporary access to a blocked app or a brief pause? You must convince Gemini with a genuine 7-sentence reason (plus optional screenshot proof).</string>
    <string name="guide_step3_tip">Gemini’s default verdict is NO, and every rejection increases your Rejection Count—making excuses harder over time.</string>
    <string name="guide_step4_title">Lock It Down in Vault</string>
    <string name="guide_step4_body">Once your rules feel right, open the Vault tab to set a strong Settings Password, activate Anti-Uninstall Protection, and export merge-safe backups.</string>
    <string name="guide_step4_tip">You can replay this guide anytime by tapping the ? icon in the top-right corner.</string>

